# Puzzle Game UI Rules (Windsurf / Cascade)

When auditing or building Unity puzzle game UI (Home, HUD, Daily Reward, Quests, Shop, Popups):

## Surface Contract (Produce before editing)
```text
surface -> user job -> states -> actions -> data source -> hierarchy -> bindings
        -> owner -> persistence -> events -> validation evidence
```

## Non-Negotiable Rules
- Definitions (ScriptableObjects/CSVs) are read-only at runtime; mutate player state models only.
- Reward claims are idempotent (validate -> apply once -> persist -> emit refresh event).
- Every interactive element must define disabled reasons and explicit visual states.
- Hierarchy structure: Screen -> SafeArea -> Header / Content / Footer / Overlay.
- Detailed specs and blueprints located in:
  `~/.agents/skills/puzzle-game-ui/references/` or `./.agents/skills/puzzle-game-ui/references/`
